  "widgets": [
    "TextWidget",
    "SelectWidget",
    "ApplicationAttachmentWidget",
    "FieldListWidget"
  ],
  "description": "Research & Related Senior/Key Person Profile (RR_KeyPerson_3_0) collects biographical and contact information for the PD/PI and other senior/key persons on a research project. Each person profile includes name, title, address, phone, email, organization, department, division, credential, and project role, plus attachment fields for biographical sketches and current & pending support.",
  "sgg_form_id": "rr_key_person_expanded",
  "notes": [
    "State/ZIP requirement: DAT shows asterisks on State and ZIP for some entries, implying they are always required. The XSD marks both as optional (State and Province are in a choice group, both minOccurs=\"0\"; ZipPostalCode is minOccurs=\"0\"). Resolution: follow the XSD. State is conditionally required when Country is USA.",
    "Department/Division maxLength: The XSD uses DepartmentNameDataTypeV2 and DivisionNameDataTypeV2, both with maxLength 100. Older versions used maxLength 30. We use the V2 constraint (100).",
    "ZIP/Postal Code maxLength: The XSD defines ZipPostalCodeDataType with maxLength 30. We will use the XSD constraint (30)."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "This form has very low volume (266 submissions/2yr, 0.01%). The Expanded variant (FID 774, 321K submissions) is the dominant version. Consider whether supporting this base version is a priority.",
    "`PersonProfileDataType` is defined in the form XSD (not the Global Library), but its child elements reference Global Library types. Validation constraints come from the Global Library.",
    "The Key Person section supports up to 7 entries (XSD maxOccurs=\"7\")",
    "State and ZIP/Postal Code show asterisks in some DAT entries but the XSD marks them as optional. The XSD is authoritative for required/optional."
  ],
